---
import ReferenceLayout from "../layouts/ReferenceLayout.astro";
---

<ReferenceLayout
	title="Patterns"
	description="Copy-owned candidate patterns in the Kinra source registry."
	current="Patterns"
>
	<header class="catalog-intro">
		<div class="catalog-intro__inner kin-frame">
			<div>
				<p class="kin-eyebrow">Source registry</p>
				<h1>Start from evidence. Keep ownership local.</h1>
			</div>
			<p class="catalog-intro__copy">
				Candidate patterns begin with a real product and are copied into the
				consumer. They are examples to adapt, not a second page generator.
			</p>
		</div>
	</header>

	<div class="catalog-section kin-frame">
		<article class="pattern-entry">
			<header class="pattern-entry__meta">
				<div>
					<span class="kin-badge" data-tone="reason">Candidate</span>
					<h2>Narrative intro</h2>
				</div>
				<p>
					An unnumbered statement-led opening with a compact evidence rail. Use
					it when a page must establish a position before presenting detail.
				</p>
			</header>
			<div class="kin-pattern-narrative-intro">
				<div class="kin-pattern-narrative-intro__statement">
					<p class="kin-eyebrow">Product position</p>
					<h3>Software should leave its operator with more agency.</h3>
				</div>
				<div class="kin-pattern-narrative-intro__support">
					<p>
						Begin with the claim that governs the page. Use the rail for
						evidence, boundaries, or orientation.
					</p>
					<dl>
						<div><dt>Owner</dt><dd>Product team</dd></div>
						<div><dt>State</dt><dd>Active</dd></div>
					</dl>
				</div>
			</div>
		</article>

		<article class="pattern-entry">
			<header class="pattern-entry__meta">
				<div>
					<span class="kin-badge" data-tone="reason">Candidate</span>
					<h2>Editorial feature</h2>
				</div>
				<p>
					A folio-led feature for one authored work. The folio changes the
					rhythm of an index without claiming that every section is a sequence.
				</p>
			</header>
			<div class="kin-pattern-editorial-feature">
				<div class="kin-pattern-editorial-feature__folio" aria-hidden="true">
					VI
				</div>
				<div class="kin-pattern-editorial-feature__copy">
					<div class="kin-cluster" data-space="compact">
						<span class="kin-badge" data-tone="reason">Essay</span>
						<span class="kin-pattern-editorial-feature__meta">12 min read</span>
					</div>
					<h3>A machine can be capable without becoming sovereign.</h3>
					<p>
						Use one restrained feature to give an authored idea room to breathe.
					</p>
					<a class="kin-button kin-button--quiet" href="#registry-guidance">
						Read the guidance
					</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</article>

		<article class="pattern-entry">
			<header class="pattern-entry__meta">
				<div>
					<span class="kin-badge" data-tone="reason">Candidate</span>
					<h2>Operations region</h2>
				</div>
				<p>
					A bounded responsibility with explicit state, actions, and inspectable
					evidence. Proven independently in Depot and the inference gateway.
				</p>
			</header>
			<section
				class="kin-pattern-operations-region"
				aria-labelledby="recent-jobs-heading"
			>
				<header class="kin-pattern-operations-region__header">
					<div>
						<div class="kin-cluster" data-space="compact">
							<h3 id="recent-jobs-heading">Recent jobs</h3>
							<span class="kin-status" data-state="success">Healthy</span>
						</div>
						<p>Inspect the latest bounded work and its recorded outcome.</p>
					</div>
					<a class="kin-button kin-button--quiet" href="#registry-guidance">
						View all jobs
					</a>
				</header>
				<div class="kin-table-wrap">
					<table class="kin-table">
						<caption>Two most recent jobs</caption>
						<thead>
							<tr>
								<th scope="col">Job</th>
								<th scope="col">State</th>
								<th scope="col">Duration</th>
							</tr>
						</thead>
						<tbody>
							<tr>
								<td>Index repository</td>
								<td
									><span class="kin-badge" data-tone="success">Complete</span
									></td
								>
								<td>12.4 s</td>
							</tr>
							<tr>
								<td>Verify release</td>
								<td><span class="kin-badge" data-tone="reason">Review</span></td
								>
								<td>48.1 s</td>
							</tr>
						</tbody>
					</table>
				</div>
			</section>
		</article>

		<section
			id="registry-guidance"
			class="pattern-entry kin-split"
			data-ratio="trail"
		>
			<div>
				<p class="kin-eyebrow">Promotion rule</p>
				<h2 class="surface-sample__title">
					Candidate after one. Stable after two.
				</h2>
			</div>
			<div class="kin-notice" data-tone="primary">
				<p class="kin-notice__title">Copy before adapting</p>
				<p class="kin-notice__body">
					Read the item guidance, copy its source, and preserve semantics. Once
					product-specific decisions enter, rename the local classes and let the
					consumer own the result.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>
	</div>
</ReferenceLayout>
